# Website 502 Guardrail

After any change that can affect live behavior (backend, frontend, deploy scripts, env wiring):

1. Verify public website health after deploy:
   - `https://www.qwertymates.com/`
   - `https://www.qwertymates.com/wall`
2. If either URL returns `502`:
   - Diagnose and fix immediately (frontend container health, NPM/openresty proxy config, upstream port mapping, missing frontend deps).
   - Re-run deploy steps needed to restore service.
   - Re-verify both URLs return non-502 (prefer `200`).
3. Do not close the task while public site still returns `502`.
4. If SSH/auth blocks remediation, report the exact blocker and the minimum credential/config needed.

Use existing project scripts first where possible (`deploy:production`, `deploy:frontend-remote:rebuild`, `remoteNpmEdgePermanentFix.mjs`, `remotePostDeployHealth.mjs`).
